    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0874" n="748" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg748"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4861: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-23T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                                1925—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 23—1:01
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>493. American consul, Swatow, states that it is reported Canton Government
                    contemplates taking over Maritime Customs, Swatow. He asks whether action
                    similar to that of the consul general, Canton, on the same question in 1923
                    should be taken.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d618-f1"/> Please instruct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
